  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Government and Civil Society Assistance on Counter-Trafficking</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will enhance the capacity of the government and civil society to provide adequate protection and assistance, as well as prevention on human trafficking for which two results have been proposed: Outcome 1. The government and civil society enhance referral mechanisms, making it possible to provide specialized assistance to victims. For these purposes, an investigation will be carried out on the number of complaints of violence presented by Venezuelan women and other migrants in Greater Santo Domingo and resolution (Output 1.1). As well at Victims of trafficking receive health services including psychological and psychiatric assistance. (Output 1.2). Outcome 2. Young students of cinema, communication and audiovisual creators have become aware of human trafficking in the Dominican Republic, creating and disseminating audiovisual pieces of communication directed and produced for a young audience. Output 2.2 Promote the creation of short films, videos and reels for social media related to human trafficking in the Dominican Republic among young film producers. Product 2.3 Promote the participation of Dominican audiovisual products in the PLURAL+ youth video festival 2023 edition to obtain more visibility.</narrative>
  </description>
